# Kimigayo OS License Information

Kimigayo OS is a container-oriented root filesystem, published as a Docker image,
composed of various software components, each with its own license. This file provides an overview of the licensing
structure, following the approach of Alpine Linux.

## License Overview

Kimigayo OS follows Alpine Linux's licensing philosophy: each component
maintains its original license, and we clearly document all licenses used.

## Component Licenses

### Core Operating System Components

| Component | License | Location |
|-----------|---------|----------|
| BusyBox | GPL-2.0-only | LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt |
| musl libc | MIT | LICENSES/musl-COPYRIGHT.txt (upstream original) |
| OpenRC (Init System) | BSD-2-Clause | LICENSES/OpenRC-LICENSE.txt (upstream original) |
| libcap (statically linked into OpenRC's start-stop-daemon and supervise-daemon) | BSD-3-Clause OR GPL-2.0-only (used under BSD-3-Clause) | LICENSES/libcap-License.txt (upstream original) |
| Linux Kernel (build scripts only; not included in the Docker image) | GPL-2.0-only | LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt |

The Docker image carries the license texts of the components it contains
in `/usr/share/licenses/`, taken from the exact upstream source archives
used for the build, together with a README that says where to get the
corresponding source. Each GitHub Release also attaches the upstream
source archives of BusyBox, musl and OpenRC.

### Kimigayo OS Original Components

| Component | License | Location |
|-----------|---------|----------|
| Build System | MIT | LICENSES/MIT.txt |
| Documentation | MIT | LICENSES/MIT.txt |
| Test Framework | MIT | LICENSES/MIT.txt |

## Directory-Specific Licenses

```
src/
├── kernel/        # GPL-2.0-only (kernel configuration and patches)
├── busybox/       # GPL-2.0-only (BusyBox configurations and patches)
└── libc/patches/  # MIT (musl patches)

tests/             # MIT
scripts/           # MIT
docs/              # MIT
```

## Third-Party Components

Kimigayo OS has no package manager by design. Software you add to the image
in your own Dockerfile (for example from an Alpine builder stage) keeps its
own license; checking and complying with it is up to you.

## License Identification

Kimigayo OS uses SPDX short identifiers for license identification,
following Alpine Linux's convention.

Common SPDX identifiers used:
- GPL-2.0-only: GNU General Public License v2.0 only
- MIT: MIT License
- BSD-2-Clause: BSD 2-Clause "Simplified" License
- BSD-3-Clause: BSD 3-Clause "New" or "Revised" License

The image label `org.opencontainers.image.licenses` is
`GPL-2.0-only AND MIT AND BSD-2-Clause AND BSD-3-Clause`.

## Compliance

### Using Kimigayo OS

You are free to:
- Use Kimigayo OS for any purpose (commercial or non-commercial)
- Modify and distribute Kimigayo OS
- Create derivative works

Subject to the terms of the individual component licenses.
If you redistribute the image (for example an image built `FROM` it),
keep `/usr/share/licenses/` and make the corresponding source available
as GPL-2.0 requires for BusyBox.

### Contributing to Kimigayo OS

By contributing to Kimigayo OS, you agree that:
- Your contributions to original components (build system, documentation, tests, etc.) will be licensed under MIT
- Your contributions to existing components will be licensed under their respective licenses
- You have the right to submit the contributions under these licenses

## Full License Texts

Full license texts are available in the `LICENSES/` directory:
- `LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt` - GNU General Public License v2.0 (BusyBox, Linux)
- `LICENSES/musl-COPYRIGHT.txt` - musl's copyright and MIT license (upstream original)
- `LICENSES/OpenRC-LICENSE.txt` - OpenRC's BSD 2-Clause license (upstream original)
- `LICENSES/libcap-License.txt` - libcap's license (upstream original)
- `LICENSES/MIT.txt` - MIT License for Kimigayo OS's own code

## Additional Information

For complete license texts and more information:
- GPL-2.0: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.html
- MIT: https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT
- BSD-2-Clause: https://opensource.org/licenses/BSD-2-Clause
- BSD-3-Clause: https://opensource.org/licenses/BSD-3-Clause

## Questions

If you have questions about licensing, please:
- Open an issue: https://github.com/Kazuki-0731/Kimigayo/issues

